{"name":"So This Is Love","hex":"#ffdef2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"this","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["The (thing) here .","Referring to oneself."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To the degree or extent indicated."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/this"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"So This Is Love? (film)","blocks":[{"text":"So This is Love? is a 1928 American silent film directed by Frank Capra. It was produced by Harry Cohn for Columbia Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/So_This_Is_Love_%281928%29.webm/330px--So_This_Is_Love_%281928%29.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/So_This_Is_Love%3F_(film)"},{"title":"So This Is Love (film)","blocks":[{"text":"So This Is Love is a 1953 American musical drama film directed by Gordon Douglas, based on the life of singer Grace Moore. The film stars Kathryn Grayson as Moore, and Merv Griffin as her boyfriend Buddy. The story chronicles Moore's rise to stardom from 1918 to February 7, 1928, when she made her debut at the Metropolitan Opera House."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cb/So_This_Is_Love_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/So_This_Is_Love_(film)"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/1280px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fraternal love (Prehispanic sculpture from 250 to 900 CE, of Huastec origin). Museum of Anthropology in Xalapa, Veracruz, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColumpio_Veracruz_059.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Gothaer_Liebespaar.jpg/500px-Gothaer_Liebespaar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Gothaer_Liebespaar.jpg/500px-Gothaer_Liebespaar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pair of Lovers. 1480–1485","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGothaer_Liebespaar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Sri_Lankan_woman_and_child.jpg/500px-Sri_Lankan_woman_and_child.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Sri_Lankan_woman_and_child.jpg/500px-Sri_Lankan_woman_and_child.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grandmother and grandchild in Sri Lanka","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASri_Lankan_woman_and_child.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimed